19.Why Collection doesn't extend Cloneable and Serializable interfaces?
Because not every collection implementation supports cloning or serialization.
Different implementations have different capabilities, so Java leaves these 
features to the implementing classes instead of forcing all collections to support them.


20. Why Map interface doesn't extend Collection interface?
Because Map stores key-value pairs, while Collection stores only individual objects.
Their structures and operations are different.
Examples:
* Collection → add(), remove()
* Map → put(), get(), remove(key)


